    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm putting together a hypertrophy plan for a client. can u explain the specific role of leucine in triggering the mTOR pathway? also need to know how a caloric surplus specifically impacts nitrogen balance for muscle protein synthesis. thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Leucine acts as a crucial signaling molecule that directly activates the mTOR pathway in response to amino acid intake. It functions as an anabolic trigger, essentially \"flipping the switch\" that initiates muscle protein synthesis. A caloric surplus provides the necessary energy substrate for muscle growth, which directly supports a positive nitrogen balance. This positive balance means your body is taking in more nitrogen from protein than it is excreting, favoring net tissue accumulation like muscle.",
      "source": "target",
