    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. so if we're looking at the lysosome part, how do we ensure the signal isn't interrupted by other metabolic stressors? like, are there factors that might prematurely shut down that mTOR signaling even if the leucine levels are high enough?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, several metabolic stressors can interrupt the mTORC1 pathway, even with high leucine intake. High levels of cortisol or severe systemic inflammation can inhibit mTOR signaling, counteracting the anabolic drive. Furthermore, deficiencies in essential amino acids beyond leucine, particularly arginine or methionine, can act as limiting factors, preventing mTORC1 from achieving peak activation. Chronic high-intensity training without adequate recovery can also induce stressors that suppress this signaling cascade.",
      "source": "target",
